  "sourceSections": [
    "Current PER Art 3.3–3.7: language, 180 EC structure, embedded development, noncredit activities, approved study plan after 45 earned EC and open-study levels/non-overlap.",
    "Current PER Appendix 2 pp79–80: quarter structure, ordinary BEP over year-3 quarters 3 and 4, 15 open EC in year 2 and 30 in year 3.",
    "Current PER Appendix 2 p83: official order Living, ICT, Robotics, each 30 EC.",
    "Current 2026–27 Psychology & Technology cohort chart: 19 common 5 EC units including two ITEC units; six named Living 5 EC units; ordinary 10 EC BEP; 45 open EC; Human Factors replaces old assumed common digital-wellbeing unit.",
    "Current PER Appendix 2 p87: BEP requires 120 EC including compulsory year 1 plus a pass in 0HV50 OR 0HV110; multidisciplinary CBL requires previously offered communication/cooperation/planning/organization skill components.",
    "Current bachelor-final-project page: individual question/report, semester-length project and preceding-quarter preparation. Optional 15 EC Innovation Space variant is not stacked with ordinary 10 EC project."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Reconstructed 28 displayed positions totaling 180 EC: 95 EC of common taught units including 10 ITEC, 30 Living technical EC, ordinary 10 EC BEP and 45 open EC. Thus 125 core EC including BEP, plus 10 ITEC and 45 open; 60 EC each year. All six Living courses have names, codes, credits and actual places rather than an unnamed 30 EC block.",
    "Generic target names no specialization. Current formal order selects Living neutrally; old Robotics-first justification was unsupported. Public pages differ in ordering and technical-course count; current adopted regulations and current cohort chart resolve those details. Living was selected before assessing UCR fit.",
    "Living engineering is Physics for Engineers, 3D Modeling Studio, Circularity and Energy Performance in the Built Environment, Healthy and Sustainable Living Environment, Building Services, and Healthful Environments: Light, Wellbeing and Biological Clock. Shared psychology/research content does not make these components optional.",
    "First year 60 fixed EC; 15 open EC in year 2 and 30 in year 3. At least 30 open EC at levels 2/3 including 15 at level 3, with non-overlapping content and an approved complete study plan after earning 45 EC; changes require approval. Two credited 5 EC ITEC units, embedded personal/professional development, five Studium Generale activities and MyFuture value seven are distinguished; the latter activities add no credits.",
    "BEP gate is 120 including compulsory year 1 AND a pass in either BRM II 0HV50 or Advanced Methods/Ethics 0HV110. A nominally completed year 2 meets the credit/BRM condition before year-3 Q3. Ordinary BEP is 10 EC and compulsory; UCR independent research is optional 15 EC outside the scheduled 180.",
    "Primary and formal sources establish a coherent current English full-time programme. NVAO 2025 is supporting identity/history, not controlling 2026 course/order evidence. Research-course pages are not substantive syllabi; research-unit themes are not universal bachelor requirements. No essential source unavailability, no source retry or deferral."
  ]
}
